# Build context for trainer/Dockerfile. The context is the repository root
# because that is where `trainer/build.sh` points the build; everything that
# is not the trainer is excluded, so a rebuild is not invalidated by a test
# run or a downloaded fixture elsewhere in the tree.
#
# `.git` IS EXCLUDED ON PURPOSE. The commit reaches the image as a build
# argument that `trainer/build.sh` reads from git on the host, never as a
# repository the image could re-interrogate. An image that can run
# `git rev-parse` is an image that can report a commit for a tree it was not
# built from.
*
!trainer/

# ...and inside that, the things that are never part of the image.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
trainer/build.sh
trainer/README.md
# The trainer's own suite lives beside the code it reads. It is not in the
# image -- the Dockerfile copies `medos_trainer/` by name, never the
# directory -- but it IS in the build context, and this file's whole purpose
# is that editing a test does not invalidate a layer.
trainer/tests/
